Jahshaka patch 0076 — the voxel bounce is a JACOBI iteration, and its dampening is 1.

SOURCE + MEDIA patch (`Components/Hlms/Pbs/{include,src}/Vct/OgreVctLighting.{h,cpp}`,
`Samples/Media/VCT/LightInjection_cs.glsl`,
`Samples/Media/VCT/LightInjection_piece_cs.any`,
`Samples/Media/VCT/LightVctBounceInject_cs.glsl`,
`Samples/Media/VCT/LightVctBounceInject_piece_cs.any`). THE PROCESS COST IS STATED
RATHER THAN AVOIDED: every tree must reset its ogre-next submodule and re-run
`irisgl/scripts/build-ogre.sh` — this one COMPILES (HlmsPbs changes), and Studio
also stages its media from the SOURCE tree (cmake/IncludeOgre.cmake). It OVERLAPS
patches 0060, 0070 and 0074 in the bounce-injection piece, so a tree that already
carries those hits `build-ogre.sh`'s "Upstream changed the patched file" on a
re-run: that is the documented per-patch reverse-check blind spot and NOT an
upstream change. The cure is the recorded one —
`git -C irisgl/thirdparty/ogre-next checkout -- . &&
git -C irisgl/thirdparty/ogre-next clean -fd` and re-run the script.

WHY (Jahshaka lane PHOTON-M2, 2026-09-17, measured; the physics read of ledger
§659, findings F-B and F-C of the 2026-09-17 render audit's PHOTON section).

THE DEFECT. `VctLighting::runBounce` propagates light by re-dispatching the
injection job over the voxel volume. The job read the RUNNING TOTAL as its base
term (`OGRE_Load3D( vctProbes[0], ... )`) and added the gather to it, so each pass
computed

    L_n = L_{n-1} + rho * G( L_{n-1} ),   i.e.   L_n = (1 + rho*G)^n * D

— a binomial series in (1 + rho*G). It never contracts: every pass re-amplifies
the first bounce's energy instead of adding a dimmer one, and the first bounce is
counted n times at n passes. Upstream held it down with a 1/pi dampening on every
pass (and a commented-out 1/(pi*(n/2+1)) beside it), and with the "more bounces
for coarser cascades" stabilisation PHOTON-M1 deleted — three fudges against one
defect.

THE FIX is the fixed point the radiance in a volume actually satisfies:

    L = D + rho * G( L ),   iterated as   L_n = D + rho * G( L_{n-1} )

which is a Jacobi iteration and contracts by rho*f per pass (f being the gather's
form factor, < 1). It needs D — the light INJECTED from the scene's lamps, before
any bounce — at every pass, and D cannot be recovered from the two ping-ponging
textures the total uses: by the second pass the direct term is the one being
overwritten. So this patch keeps D in its own volume:

  * `VctLighting::mLightDirect`, one RGBA8_UNORM_SRGB 3D texture per cascade at
    mip 0 only (the bounce reads it with a Load3D at the voxel it is writing,
    never filtered), created and destroyed with `mLightBounce` in
    `setAllowMultipleBounces` — a volume that cannot bounce has no use for it.
    +8 MB at 128^3, +1 MB at 64^3, per cascade, in DEVICE memory.
  * the light-injection job writes it as a SECOND UAV in the same dispatch that
    writes the total, under a new `vct_keep_direct` property (one extra image
    store per voxel; no copy, no second dispatch, no encoder switch, and nothing
    on the CPU). The property and both slots are re-asserted per injection for
    the same reason `correct_area_light_shadows` is: "VCT/LightInjection" is ONE
    HlmsComputeJob shared by name by every VctLighting in the process.
  * the bounce job takes `directVoxel` at the texture unit after every probe
    array (so no existing slot index moves) and uses it as the base term.
  * `iterationDampening` becomes 1.0, which is the physics: the six-cone gather
    is a weighted mean over a cosine-ish set — an estimate of E/pi — and the
    bounced radiance of a Lambertian surface is rho*E/pi = rho*G. No further
    factor exists to apply. (HlmsPbs consumes the same gather as `envColourD`
    with no division of its own: `200.BRDFs_piece_ps.any:305`, Rd =
    envColourD * albedo.) The pass index `runBounce` took for upstream's
    per-iteration dampening goes with it: every pass of a Jacobi iteration is the
    same operator.

MEASURED (spikes/photon-m2, `m2-bounceC.js` — a closed 5 m cube of albedo 0.791,
one lamp, the irradiance field off so the picture is the cone term alone; the
per-pass INCREMENT of a 25-probe mean and the RATIO of consecutive increments,
which must be about rho for a contracting series):

    arm                                   increments        ratios
    base (1/pi + accumulating)         0.88  0.52  0.60    0.59  1.15
    dampening 1 alone (0075 as held)   2.00  1.88  1.96    0.94  1.04
    this patch (Jacobi + 1)            3.64  1.60  0.40    0.44  0.25

The base and the 0075-alone arms do not contract (the third increment is as large
as the second, or larger — the binomial signature); this patch's contracts
monotonically, at 0.44 and 0.25 against rho*f. The same rig at a quarter of the
lamp's intensity reads 0.50 and 0.455.

THE SELFTEST: this patch plus 0077 moves `--engine-selftest` from
`277ba3c2…` to `ebe346e1…` (54,228 of 65,536 pixels by at most 6/255, every
changed channel DARKER — the default scene's cone-lit diffuse is no longer pi
times too bright). 0077 alone reads `8254977e…`; this patch is the difference
between them.
